    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • 2027 Toyota Crown Signia Gets GT-S Concept Treatment for SEMA, Becomes a Sleek Wagon\nMan Buys New 2024 Corvette Z06 Convertible for $152,415, Drives 1,200 Miles, Sells for $115,000\n21 photos\nPhoto: Cars & Bids\nHere's yet another C8 Z06 that got bought well. Basically, a $37,000 discount for a barely-driven Z06 Convertible, meaning the buyer avoided that steep initial depreciation while acquiring a supercar with a super spec. The seller? Owning this car cost them approximately $31 per mile, on top of their initial $152,415 investment.\nMyself, I don't mind the $115,000 valuation, especially when you factor in the Z06 Ultimate Performance and Carbon Fiber Aero packages. Would I have preferred it if this was a 3LZ model? Yes, absolutely. But there's nothing wrong with a good 2LZ, especially if it comes with the optional front-axle lift system, which this does.\nAlso, this is a convertible, not a coupe. I know that doesn't matter to some people - I think you can be just as happy with the coupe, since the top comes down. But others will always prefer the ability to drop top electrically. It's faster, more efficient, and let's face it, more practical.\nIn terms of visuals, this Z06 is very pretty to say the least. I love the Ceramic Matrix Gray colorway, which tends to look white depending on lighting. It also allows for a high contrast look once paired with various dark trim pieces, like you get with the aforementioned Carbon Fiber Aero package.\nOther highlights include the 20\" front and 21\" rear Spider Design forged wheels, leather upholstery, power-adjustable heated and ventilated GT bucket seats, the Z07 suspension, LED headlights, a head-up display, Brembo brakes, black exhaust tips, Torch Red seat belts, cruise control, heated steering wheel, wireless CarPlay and Android Auto, dual-zone automatic climate control, and quite a bit more.\nYou also get a wide range of electronic driver aids, such as rear park assist, rear cross traffic alert, side blind zone alert, the Intellibeam-Auto high beam system, a following distance indicator, forward collision alert, lane keep assist with lane departure warning, and automatic emergency braking.\nPhoto: Cars & Bids The options alone cost nearly $25,000. Among them the $9,000 Z06 Ultimate Performance package and the $8,500 Carbon Aero pack. 2LZ or no 2LZ, this is a lot of car for $115k. A lot of supercar, that is.\nAs for performance, it all comes down to the mid-mounted 5.5-liter LT6 V8 engine. It's putting down 670 horsepower and 460 lb-ft of torque, with everything getting sent to the rear wheels via an eight-speed dual-clutch automatic transmission.\nI'm going to be straight with you guys. I don't recall a whole lot of nicer Z06 Convertibles for this type of money. I'm not saying this is any kind of a world record, but it's pretty solid value. One car I recall is this 2024 Z06 Coupe with 1,500 miles on the clock that sold for $110,500. Cheaper but, again, a Coupe, not a Convertible.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nchevrolet corvette z06 convertible corvette z06 convertible corvette z06 Corvette Chevrolet Chevrolet Corvette auction used cars\nAbout the author: Sergiu Tudose\nSergiu got to experience both American and European car \"scenes\" at an early age (his father drove a Ford Fiesta XR2 supermini in the 80s). After spending over 15 years at local and international auto publications, he's starting to appreciate comfort behind the wheel more than raw power and acceleration. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1958 Chevrolet Bel Air Gets First Cleaning in Decades, Morphs Into Stunning Survivor",
